Wooooo!

I just downloaded the most recent nightly build of
SeaMonkey, the "better than Firefox" tabbed browser
from the Mozilla people, and immediately found a
spiffy new feature.

Before, hovering over the tab got the web page's
windows title bar for that page shown in tool tip
style, useful for the case where you have so many
tabs you get no clue what they are by looking at
them.

Now, you get a 3"x5" (maybe) super-thumbnail of the
would-be-visible portion of the tab's whole web
page popped up.

This has a coolness factor too high to measure.

http://www.mozilla.org/developer/#builds

